{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UccoYnzSNvnfKpxnYhT76m","type":"tool_result","content":"436\t**3.** Why do ephemeral containers exist as a separate API mechanism rather than as an ordinary edit to a Pod's spec?\n437\t\n438\t- A) Because ephemeral containers need a different container runtime\n439\t- B) Because a Pod's container list cannot be added to once the Pod exists\n440\t- C) Because ephemeral containers are scheduled to a different node\n441\t- D) Because RBAC cannot grant `update` on Pods\n442\t\n443\t**4.** You run `kubectl debug <pod> --copy-to=<pod>-debug --image=ubuntu`. Immediately afterward, what is the state of the original Pod?"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db8806b3-f099-42bb-9304-df6ee5a40e0d","uuid":"754f7030-a8b0-43af-aace-9b19da813d55","timestamp":"2026-08-31T12:15:58.629Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-16\\draft-v1.md","content":"**3.** Why do ephemeral containers exist as a separate API mechanism rather than as an ordinary edit to a Pod's spec?\n\n- A) Because ephemeral containers need a different container runtime\n- B) Because a Pod's container list cannot be added to once the Pod exists\n- C) Because ephemeral containers are scheduled to a different node\n- D) Because RBAC cannot grant `update` on Pods\n\n**4.** You run `kubectl debug <pod> --copy-to=<pod>-debug --image=ubuntu`. Immediately afterward, what is the state of the original Pod?","numLines":8,"startLine":436,"totalLines":1224}}}
